WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.270
My nephew got a voice note last month.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.100
It was his mum's voice, worried:

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.540
“I've lost my phone, send airtime to

4
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.420
this new number, quickly!”

5
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.060
It wasn't her: it was a copy of her voice,

6
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.120
made from a video she had posted.

7
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.660
Today: how AI makes scams more convincing,

8
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.500
and the habits that still beat them.

9
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.700
You already know the old signs of

10
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.800
a scam: a rush, a prize, a

11
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.760
strange link, bad spelling.

12
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.210
AI changes some of them.

13
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.740
It writes perfect

14
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.620
messages in any language.

15
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.980
And it can copy a voice or a

16
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.840
face from what people post.

17
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.400
Scammers also use what you share.

18
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.160
Your school, your friends' names,

19
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.160
your team: AI can mix them into a

20
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.780
message that feels personal.

21
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.300
But a message that knows you is not

22
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.300
proof it comes from someone you know.

23
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.670
Then there are fake AI apps, like

24
00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.890
“free premium” chatbots.

25
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.620
Some steal your login or

26
00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.420
read your messages.

27
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.240
Get apps only from the official

28
00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.400
store, and check who made them

29
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.580
and what they ask for.

30
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.740
The best defence doesn't

31
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.320
depend on spotting the fake.

32
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.240
It's a habit: verify on a second channel.

33
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.770
Hang up, and call back on the

34
00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:26.850
number you already have.

35
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.620
Or ask something only the

36
00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.820
real person would know.

37
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.370
Quick check!

38
00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.150
A message from your best friend's number

39
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.770
says: “Send me the six-digit code you

40
00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.370
just got, it's for the game.”

41
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:40.720
What do you do?

42
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:42.860
Don't send it.

43
00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.140
A code is a key, and nobody

44
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.140
should ask for it.

45
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.620
Your friend's account may have been

46
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.960
taken over, so check another way.

47
00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.120
For copied voices, agree a family

48
00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.220
code word, never posted online.

49
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.500
If a call or voice note asks for money

50
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.500
in a hurry, ask for the word.

51
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.040
A copied voice can't know it.

52
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.400
In the app, a stranger calls you

53
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.880
during break and asks for your code.

54
00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.370
Answer the way many people would,

55
00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.410
and see how fast it goes wrong.

56
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:19.340
Then take the call again, refuse,

57
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.080
and spot each trick he uses.

58
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.160
What if you were tricked?

59
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.750
Don't hide it: tell an adult, change

60
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.330
your password, and call the bank or

61
00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.210
mobile money agent straight away.

62
00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.270
The sooner you act, the more you can save.

63
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.330
Your turn.

64
00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.990
A voice note sounds exactly like your

65
00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:46.630
uncle: he's stuck and needs mobile money

66
00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:47.030
now.

67
00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.060
What's your first move?

68
00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:53.380
Call his usual number, or ask for the code

69
00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.820
word, because a voice can be copied.

70
00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.510
Remember: codes are keys,

71
00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.030
so never share them.

72
00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.520
Get apps from the official store.

73
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.310
And verify on a second channel.

74
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.320
Try it tomorrow: agree a family code

75
00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.560
word at home, and never post it.

76
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.680
Then check the apps on your phone, or

77
00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.060
a family phone with its owner.

78
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.020
Delete any you don't recognise, or

79
00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.540
that ask for far too much.
